# Normalize line endings so local tooling matches CI on every platform.
#
# oxfmt (`pnpm format:check`) requires LF. Without this file, Windows clones get
# CRLF on checkout via core.autocrlf, so the check fails locally on files that
# pass on the Linux CI runners. `text=auto` lets git detect text vs binary and
# `eol=lf` pins the working-tree ending regardless of each contributor's
# core.autocrlf setting.
#
# There are no Windows-only files in this repo. If one is ever added (*.bat,
# *.cmd, *.ps1), give it an `eol=crlf` exception here.
* text=auto eol=lf
